On our way out, Esher rejoined us, telling of an
intriguing conversation he had just had with one
of the locals. Before he could go on, the 
unsavory man we had seen before stepped outside 
and pushed his way into our midst. Bergon, 
flushed with anger, grabbed his sword, but Esher
held him back. "This is the man I was telling 
you about," he said with no particular 
enthusiasm.

"I am called Minar, and I have travelled often 
in the Outlands. You are in great danger, 
whether you know it or not. If you will have me,
I offer you my services." Minar's eyes flickered
with a disturbing light, but saying nothing, we 
awaited the decision of Bergon.
 
 
 
 
