It was mid-afternoon when we left Lavos, heading
south. The road, which soon narrowed to a simple
foot path, wound its way down into a deep 
canyon, surrounded by sheer walls. After a short
time, we found ourselves at a fork in the path, 
the left branch leading east along the foothills
and the right one continuing down the valley to 
the south. Both appeared desolate and poorly 
traveled. I wondered which path Garlimon's party
had taken, and how near they had come to 
reaching Astrix. And then, a cold, bone-dry wind
arose from the north, filling me with dread.
