Minar was sent out to explore the area around 
us. What he found brought little cheer.

"A rock cairn," he said, leading us to a shaded 
spot beneath a grove of stately oaks, "I am 
certain this was not here last summer, when I 
camped in this same spot."

Minar's words were ominous - whatever was buried
here had not lain long in the earth. Fearful 
over what we might find, we decided to dig up 
whatever remains lay there. It was not long 
before we found what we were after - three sets 
of human remains, their bodies mangled and 
bloodied, yet covered with their own cloaks.

"Garlimon's party!" cried Bergon. "But there are
only three, not four...."

"And that is but part of the mystery," replied 
Praxix, "Who, I wonder, took the time to bury 
them? Surely not the assassins that tortured and
killed them."
