"We have journeyed from Lavos, as you say; we 
seek the Wizard Astrix, to seek his aid."

"Fools! There is no Wizard, there is only the 
Enemy - and he is strong - too strong for the 
likes of you!"

"And how do you know this?" Bergon demanded.

The hermit retreated to his stool, and sat again
in the corner. "I know nothing!" he said, and 
sighed deeply.
