We shuffled out of the hut, and Garlimon hobbled
to the door as we made our way back to our path.
"Begone!" he cried, and threw a small leather 
bag at our feet. "Perhaps this will help you 
where you are going!" He started to cackle 
madly, and began to chant in a sing-song 
fashion. "The water that heals, the fire 
reveals, the earth..." He was babbling 
incoherently now, and soon slammed the door 
behind us. Curious as to what we had been given,
I bent down and picked up the bag.

"He was a great man; the misfortunes of his 
party are a heavy load to bear," Bergon said, 
and we made our way in silence to the high 
plain.
