Descending from the high plain, we headed toward
the near shore of the lake. Nearing the halfway 
point, we stopped at a wide stream whose waters 
careened down the slope and into the lake below.
The sky was dark, and a storm threatened.

"Look!" Praxix cried, pointing toward the 
lowering clouds. For a long time we saw nothing,
but soon a great, white bird emerged from the 
cloud base and soared overhead in graceful 
spirals.

"I have seen nothing like it," Bergon said, as 
the bird disappeared into the eastern sky.
