As we stood, unsure of which way to proceed, I 
was asked by Praxix to bring out the map we had 
bought at Webba's. Removing it from my pack, I 
unfolded it and handed it to him.

"Yes!" he said, knowingly. "There is the river 
we crossed with the forest behind it, and the 
mountains - here - lie ahead of us."

"But which path is the right one?" I asked, 
pointing at the bewildering array of marks which
adorned each and every fork.

"I'm afraid we cannot know," Praxix admitted. 
"Perhaps they are all good paths," he added, 
with little conviction.
