Increasingly apprehensive, we made our way 
slowly down the passage.

Ahead of us, we could make out muffled noises 
which were coming nearer with each passing 
moment.
ProceedProceedProceedProceedProceed
Reaching toward our weapons, we moved forward at
a snail's pace; the sounds grew louder and 
seemed to come from all around us!

Our assailants had finally arrived; Dwarves they
were, and heavily armed. We joined in a tight 
circle, weapons drawn, and waited for the 
onslaught. But they did not attack; rather, 
their leader, somewhat taller and having about 
him an air of superiority, strode forward.

"What business have you here in Reth a-Zar?" he 
demanded. "Come, speak quickly, for we have no 
patience with strangers!" Under his breath, 
Praxix repeated the strange words - 'Reth 
a-Zar'; they held some great meaning for our 
Wizard-friend, but for us they spoke only of 
hopelessness and despair.
