We continued our march through the long passage.
"We have come nearly to the eastern extent of 
the Reth a-Zar, where the Bern i-Fen leads to 
the Old Forest," Hurth said.

"That sounds fine to me," I exclaimed, "What I 
wouldn't give to see the sunshine again!"

Bergon laughed, as did Praxix, but there was 
another sound also, cold and rumbling, like 
distant thunder; and it came from before us.

"I know not what lies before us," Hurth said, 
"yet I know that many evils, having long 
inhabited the deepest places of the earth, now 
boldly tread even on the Dwarves' hallowed 
halls."
