Hurth was asked by Praxix about the true story 
of the Dwarf Gates. Hurth replied eagerly, 
pleased to give us a taste of Dwarvish history.

"Our fathers built four gates, each leading to 
one of the outposts of the world. The Bern 
i-Lav, where you entered, was our link to the 
plains of Lavos. The Bern i-Fen, at the opposite
end of the Long Road, leads to the forests of 
the Elves. And the Bern i-Zar leads upwards to 
the high mountains of Thur."

"And what of the fourth gate?" Bergon asked.

"Of the fourth gate, the Bern i-Lan," Hurth 
replied gravely, "it is not spoken. Perhaps it 
no longer exists; this is what we Dwarves fear 
most."
