Hurth approached the door and spoke a Dwarvish 
command of opening. The massive door obliged 
without a sound, and we entered a large 
vestibule; the door closed behind us, becoming 
invisible.

"These Dwarvish doors take some getting used 
to!" I said, thinking of the gate through which 
we entered these caverns.

"Do not be alarmed," said Hurth. "Watch!" Hurth 
called out a command, but no door appeared. He 
laughed nervously, then called out a few dozen 
more foreign words the last few of which sounded
rather more like expletives than commands.

"Well?" Esher prompted, but Hurth was deep in 
thought. Bergon, trying his best to control his 
temper, paced to the center of the vestibule, 
and looked down the dark corridors which led off
to our left and right.
