Praxix raised his arm before him, and from his 
crooked forefinger shot a small ball of fire, 
illuminating the cavern walls as it sped into 
the gloom.

"Well, that was useful!" Esher said, in his most
sarcastic voice. I was sure that Praxix would 
respond with some clever retort, when his face 
became contorted with fear. "Down!" he shouted, 
pushing us to the ground.

"What the...?" started Bergon, catching sight of
the ball of flame that raced toward us. As it 
continued down the far corridor, we pulled 
ourselves to our feet. "It would seem," Praxix 
said blankly, wiping the medium textured violet 
residue from his fingers, "that following these 
corridors will be a tiring proposition!"

Then, casting his gaze upward, he saw, in the 
dim afterglow of the fireball, a narrow ledge 
not two dozen feet above us. "I suggest we march
that way!", he said, and raised his crooked 
forefinger toward the darkening image.
