Praxix now drew some magical powder from his 
cloak, motioned Bergon a few steps to his left, 
then cast the preparation onto him. He climbed 
into the air, coming finally to a landing which 
he grabbed tightly onto (for fear of going even 
higher!) Once the elevation spell had worn off, 
he released his grip on the rock slab and pulled
himself to his feet. Lowering the rope which I 
had thrown up to him, Bergon brought the others 
up to the landing where he stood.

At the landing was a passage, and this we 
followed until we came finally to a fork; both 
left and right paths looked evil and foreboding.
Perhaps it was some illusion or trick of the 
eye, but the walls along the right-hand path 
seemed to glow eerily.
