Using his staff for light, Praxix continued down
the tunnel in the direction of camp. Casually 
scanning the walls, he recognized the plant that
almost completely surrounded him: westflake! He 
gathered some of the root for Minar, placing it 
in his cloak. He continued down the tunnel, 
coming eventually to a ladder carved into the 
earth and rising into a hollowed-out tree stump!
The sound of a voice (or was it voices) could be
heard just above, and Praxix eagerly pulled 
himself up the ladder.

***

"Tag, you search the forest to the north," 
Bergon said, and that was what I did, though I 
was filled with apprehension at the thought of 
exploring on my own.

But the forest was beautiful, and the air cool 
and fresh. Up ahead, the sound of flowing water 
could be heard ever more clearly, and I followed
that sound until I came upon a small stream, 
which took off at an angle to my path.
