We called out for V'ren, who quickly arrived at 
the side of the pool. Then, taking me by the 
hand, she led us through twisty forest paths 
until we reached a small clearing. "This is the 
Elf Home," she said, without words. "Home of our
Mothers for all the long ages."

I looked up, and was amazed to see the trees 
filled with what seemed to be hammocks. "This is
where we live - in the trees," V'ren explained.

We talked among ourselves, marvelling at this 
ancient place, when three Elves rushed into the 
clearing, and their cries filled our ears. 
"Fire!" they said. "The great flame approaches!"

Across the way, an older Elf clambered down from
his tree-hammock. "Awake! Awake!" he cried, and 
dozens of Elves were soon marching to the north,
where smoke could be seen in the treetops.
