from the junction. But the relief was 
short-lived, as the wide path soon narrowed to 
the point that we could march only in single 
file. Two sounds could clearly be heard: the 
sound of rushing water from somewhere nearby, 
and far more ominously, the pounding footfalls 
of approaching orcs.

"I fear the orcs are somewhat more clever than 
we anticipated," Praxix said, trying not to 
appear disturbed. "Let us hope there is some 
escape for us farther along the way."
