the miner interrupted. "Before I answer your 
questions, I've got one of my own," he said. 
"What are you doing in my mine?"

Bergon replied with a condensed version of the 
truth, as the miner listened in scornful 
disbelief.

"Just plain stupid," was his conclusion; he spat
on the ground and continued, "Go on, ask your 
questions and get out. I've got lots more work 
to do!"
