"So what exactly is it you're mining here?" 
asked Bergon, who was trying to get a better 
look at the miner's sack.

"Lots of things," he said. "The stuff of the 
earth, if you know what I mean." He reached into
his sack and pulled out a few large rocks. "Now 
this here is mostly gold, but I reckon you've 
seen that before. And this," he said, holding up
a shiny black stone, "is obsidian - fetch a good
price for that in Zan, I figure."

He rummaged through his sack, dropping some 
small red rocks on the ground, and announced, 
"That's about it, so far anyway. But I've found 
silver, platinum, even a couple of diamonds 
once! You never know what you'll find in these 
walls!"
