After a moment's thought, Bergon selected Hurth 
to make the descent. Praxix removed the tiniest 
amount of earth and fire essences from his pouch
and applied them to Hurth's cloak, causing it to
glow faintly. "At least you will have some light
for your descent," he said.

Taking out our rope, we securely tied one end 
around Hurth's waist, and slowly lowered him 
down into the darkened hole. When we had reached
the rope's end, Hurth was still not at the 
bottom.

"It would seem to be about ten feet down from 
here," he said. "I can't tell much else for 
now."
 
 
 
 
