"Time to do some exploring," Hurth said. Then, 
leaving our view, Hurth spent a seeming eternity
scouting out his surroundings. When he again 
became visible, each of us breathed a sigh of 
relief.

"I've found a friend," he said, smiling, "an old
friend!" He held up to our view a decayed human 
skull. "Quite the worse for wear. I would say 
he's been here quite a few years. Found this 
alongside," he said, tossing up an iron key. 
"Nothing else here, I'm afraid."

"What do you think?" Bergon asked, holding up 
the key.

"Perhaps he dropped the key, then went in after 
it and got trapped," I suggested.
