Hurth took a tentative step forward and touched 
the polished stone with his hand. Breathlessly, 
he lifted the lid and stood there, frozen with 
fear. "I cannot believe it," he said in a 
perfect monotone.

It was impossible, and to this day we have not 
found an explanation for what we discovered 
within: a Dwarvish body, perfectly preserved 
through the long years. He wore a long, white 
robe which appeared to glisten in the light of 
Praxix' staff. Around his neck, a round white 
stone hung at the end of a golden chain.

"Cedrith!" gasped Hurth, stumbling backward.
