We returned to the side of the river with our 
goal accomplished. The path here continued to 
run along the river's edge, and we followed it 
for many hours, as it wound its way upward, 
finally rising out of the caverns and into the 
open air.

We had emerged from the caverns only a few miles
south of the falls we had just barely escaped 
earlier in our journey. Before us lay a forest 
that was quite a bit older and darker than the 
one in which the Elves lived.
