As we continued, the forest grew increasingly 
dark and foreboding. The stately stands of pine 
and alder were gone, replaced by shorter, more 
twisted trees that seemed to choke the very life
out of the forest. A rustling noise filled our 
ears, and the trees writhed with a hypnotic 
motion, though the air was still, with no hint 
of a breeze.
