penetrate, and Bergon finally unsheathed his 
sword, hacking at the undulating branches. But 
the branches did not break; they sloughed off, 
falling to the ground in a pool of steamy green 
slime. The air was now steamy, and the wavy 
branches taunted us, goading us onward into 
their unrelenting grasp.
