Hoping at least to get some useful information 
from this root-bound nuisance, Praxix asked, "Do
you know where these paths lead?"

"Why, of course; on the left is the Milky Way, 
right in front of you is the road to ruin, and 
here on the right is the garden path," the tree 
replied matter-of-factly.

"I don't suppose you have a preference," Praxix 
asked with little hope.

"No, I've never felt the need for one," the tree
responded, "I'm not going much of anywhere." And
with that, he shook a few branches to indicate 
the limits of his movement.
