AcceptAcceptAcceptAccept
There was no apparent harm in this, so Praxix 
assented.

Praxix-->AcceptDecline 
"Name's Umber," the man said by way of belated 
introduction, "and I'm pleased to meet you." He 
put out his hand, and smiled broadly, reminding 
Praxix of the used merchandise sellers whom he 
despised so deeply.

"What have I done?" Praxix asked the heavens 
with upraised hands. "Trapped up here with... 
with..." He paused, choosing his words with 
care. "With my party out there," he said, moving
his hands across the broad expanse of forest 
that lay before him.

"Don't they know you're here?" Umber asked, once
again smiling.

A brilliant thought crossed Praxix' mind, then 
left as quickly as it had entered. "No, we were 
separated in the fog this morning."

"Ah. Did I hear you say 'trapped'?" Umber asked,
smile waning.

"Yes, trapped. The bridge collapsed as I crossed
it. So unless you're up for a swim in the 
moat...," was Praxix' reply, and it left Umber 
at a loss for words and smiles.
