It wasn't long before we were on our way toward 
what we presumed to be Praxix' location. The 
forest had thinned out somewhat, and we walked 
with ease through the leaf-covered ground. 
Bergon was in the lead, and our spirits were 
high.

But this was not to be a pleasant afternoon. 
Just a minute after entering this forest, Hurth 
began complaining of difficult breathing. As his
breathing became increasingly labored, he soon 
found it too strenuous to walk, and finally he 
collapsed beneath a tree, wheezing loudly.
