Esher now rushed over to Hurth and began to 
examine him, quickly coming to the conclusion 
that our Dwarvish friend was suffering from a 
severe allergic reaction, a life-threatening one
at that.

Fortunately, Esher had found some hawkbane 
earlier in our journey, and he forced our 
stricken friend to swallow the bitter root, 
which he did with great difficulty. But the 
hawkbane worked within seconds, and Hurth was 
soon back on his feet, though surprised by the 
suddenness of the attack.

"Have you ever been outside of your caverns?" 
Esher asked.

"Never," Hurth replied. "It is generally 
forbidden."

"Then that is the explanation," Esher responded.
"Your body is entirely unused to the spores and 
pollens in the air. It is a good thing I've got 
an ample supply of the remedy."
