The situation appeared grim, and I wondered if 
there might be anything in my pack which would 
help. To my astonishment, I came up literally 
empty-handed, for as I pulled my hand from the 
pack, I found it to be entirely transparent. And
then I put two pieces together: the disappearing
miner and the pieces of red rock that had 
inadvertantly fallen from his sack.

Reaching back into the pack, I noticed that some
powder had been scraped off one of the red 
rocks. "A magical reagent!" I said to myself, 
proud to have made such an important discovery. 
"Praxix will be pleased - if we find him, that 
is."
