Determined to save Bergon, I took one of the red
rocks from my pack and pummelled it into a fine 
powder which I then spread across my body. In a 
matter of moments, I was completely invisible! 
Not knowing how long the powder would work, I 
moved quickly into the heart of the orcs' camp.

It took quite a while, but I finally found 
Bergon, bound and gagged inside a tent alongside
the cooking area.

"Psst! Bergon!" I whispered from just beside his
right ear. He nearly jumped out of his bonds at 
the sound of my voice.

"Mmgmm rumggm," he said frantically through his 
gag.

"Calm down," I said, "I'm just invisible." It 
didn't take long to free him, but we now faced a
difficult decision.
