A hiding place was nowhere to be found in this 
open plain, and all eyes turned to Praxix. A 
seeming eternity passed before he spoke.

"None of my spells will protect us, but..." He 
paused again, tapping his head with his staff as
if trying to unjam some piece of mental 
machinery. "Now that I think of it, I can recall
that one combination of essences produces a kind
of fog or mist. All I need do is figure out 
which two..."

The dark shadow lengthened as we breathlessly 
awaited the results of Praxix' magic.
 
 
 
 
