"Are you thinking what I'm thinking?" I said, 
turning to Praxix.

He was; in fact, he had already taken a red rock
from his pack and powdered it, taking care to 
avoid spilling it on himself. Then, he stood up 
and, placing himself between me and the other 
table, spread the dust over me. In a moment, I 
had vanished, and it appears nobody noticed. 
Praxix nonchalantly took his seat, and I headed 
over to the neighboring table to find out what I
could.

The group was in conversation; there were four 
men at the table; of these, there was only one 
whose face I could not see.

The man farthest away was now speaking. "...less
concerned about what you desire than about our 
reward. This is not a barbarian land like the 
northern hinterlands, with all respect. If we 
get caught, there will be hell to pay."
 
 
 
 
