The man at my left was still speaking, though I 
had missed some of what he had been saying. 
"...easy, but we spoke to them all, except for 
the drunkard Bendor, of course, but he hasn't 
been sober in over a week. Don't worry. If they 
leave by boat, I guarantee they will have an 
unpleasant voyage, to say the least."

The hidden man had the final words. "Succeed in 
your task," he said, "and your reward will befit
they who walk with kings. I must leave Zan at 
once, but I shall return in three days. I know I
have chosen well here today."

And that ended the conversation. The men stood 
up and left the tavern in a group, and it seemed
they protected the fourth man, the one whose 
face was hidden from me, making it impossible 
for me to get a closer look.

Fearing to be seen materializing, I slipped out 
of the tavern and around back, waiting there 
until I was reasonably opaque. I received scant 
attention as I returned to the tavern, and in a 
moment I was seated with the others, telling 
them what I had learned.
