Lying beside Praxix was his pouch of magical 
powders, and, as discreetly as I could, I picked
them up. Inside the pouch were a number of 
smaller bags. Of these, only the reagents were 
simple to recognize. But the others numbered 
eight, not four as I had expected. Each of these
bags held a powder, and these powders were of 
different colors and consistencies.

I tried to think what Praxix would do, what he 
was trying to do, when he was struck down by 
this messenger of evil. I thought about the 
various spells that Praxix had cast during our 
journey, but none seemed powerful enough. 
Perhaps Praxix had a spell to call forth a bolt 
of lightning, but even so, I had no idea of 
which combination of essences would produce it?

"Let me see," the demon went on, "Who, do you 
suppose, should receive this lesson?"
